    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Shah Commission was set up in April 1966 to demarcate the boundaries for the creation of Haryana.",
        "Haryana shares its borders with 5 states (Punjab, Himachal Pradesh, Rajasthan, Uttar Pradesh, Uttarakhand) and 2 Union Territories (Delhi, Chandigarh).",
        "Key state symbols frequently asked: State Animal is the Blackbuck, State Bird is the Black Francolin, State Tree is Peepal, and State Flower is Lotus."
      ],
      "id": "favvrjf"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Haryana was constituted as the 17th state of the Indian Union on 1 November 1966 under the Punjab Reorganisation Act.",
        "Chandigarh acts as the shared administrative capital for both Haryana and Punjab.",
        "The state consists of 6 administrative divisions: Ambala, Faridabad, Gurugram, Hisar, Rohtak, and Karnal.",
        "Faridabad is the most populous district, while Sirsa is the largest district by geographical area.",
        "The official language of the state is Hindi, with Punjabi recognized as an additional official language."
      ],
      "id": "a06dcs7"
    }
